<!-- The mission heroes (#1335, Phase 2 of #1325): the Long Defeat's own Aragorn, Legolas and Gimli, and the free heroes of the Helm's Deep
     story mission in a campaign (#1366). SubModule.xml loads this file for Campaign, CampaignStoryMode and CustomGame. They are copies of the
     named companions (named_companions/named_companions.xml: the same face, skills and name key, so the existing translations apply), kept
     apart so that no campaign Hero ever stands behind a mission agent and a balance edit here never reaches the named companions (the
     campaign Heroes). It does reach the second user of these characters, the Helm's Deep story mission of a campaign. There is no <Hero>
     entry: in a campaign IsHero reads false, in a Custom Game is_hero makes the engine refuse a take-over and the shop's upgrade filter skip
     them. level="36" gives battle tier 7 with no Hero (BasicCharacterObject.GetBattleTier), the tier a Custom Game gives a hero. The level
     does more. In a Custom Game GetPower rises from 0.50 to 5.49 (BasicCharacterObject.GetPower: 0.2 + (Level + 10)^2 * 0.0025) and
     SkillFactor from 1/32 to 1 (Min(Level, 32) / 32); the AI's formation power sums the cached power, and the agent's position error
     reads SkillFactor. In a campaign GetPower and GetBattlePower follow the tier (CharacterObject.GetPower, GetBattlePower).
     occupation="Wanderer" without is_template keeps them out of the companion pool and the encyclopedia. is_obsolete keeps them out of
     the Custom Battle pickers. No horse: a mounted share of a tenth or more switches a formation to mounted spacing, and one rider is a third of the heroes' group. The
     engine wields the first weapon slot at the spawn (Mission.SpawnTroopWithAgentBuildData), so Legolas's bow is in the first slot. A name change needs a new
     {=key}, because a copied key shows the companion's translation. -->
